We need to produce SHACL shapes that capture the requirement: "In the event that a structural member spans across the boundary of a hull area, the largest hull area factor is to be used in the scantling determination of the member."

We have ontology terms: structuralMember class, hasSpannedHullArea object property from structuralMember to hullAreaValue, hullAreaFactor property from hullAreaValue to QuantityValue, selectedHullAreaFactor from structuralMember to QuantityValue. Also hullAreaBoundary is datatype property but ownership unresolved.

The requirement indicates a constraint: for each structuralMember that has a spanned hull area (or possibly multiple), the selectedHullAreaFactor should be the maximum of the hullAreaFactor values of those spanned hull areas.

We need to express this in SHACL: For each ?sm a structuralMember, retrieve all linked hullAreaValue via hasSpannedHullArea (maybe multiple). For each such hull area, get its hullAreaFactor (a QuantityValue). The selectedHullAreaFactor of the structuralMember must equal the maximum of those hullAreaFactor quantities.

SHACL cannot easily compute max numeric values, but we can use sh:or with sh:equals constraints? However SHACL 2.0 supports sh:hasValue, sh:property constraints etc. There's sh:qualifiedValueShape with sh:count constraints but not max.

We could express as a SPARQL constraint that verifies that selectedHullAreaFactor's numeric value equals the max of hullAreaFactor numeric values for spanned areas. Use the numeric and unit predicates defined in quantityEncoding: numericValue and unit.

Thus, we need a sh:NodeShape targeting structuralMember (owner_class). However note termOwners: hasSpannedHullArea owner is structuralMember, but shape target must be structuralMember class.

The target class: https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#structuralMember.

We need to embed the SPARQL expression referencing the QUDT numericValue and unit.

We should use sh:targetClass.

Define a property shape for selectedHullAreaFactor perhaps, but we can just have a sh:SPARQLConstraint with a SELECT that returns violating nodes if condition not met.

We must include prefixes: sh, rdf, rdfs, xsd, qudt, nltl (maybe.

Define shape:

 _:StructuralMemberHullAreaFactorConstraint a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetClass nltl:structuralMember ;
    sh:message "Selected hull area factor must be the largest hull area factor among spanned hull areas." ;
    sh:sparql [
        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
        sh:prefixes ... ;
        sh:select """SELECT $this WHERE {
            $this nltl:hasSpannedHullArea ?area .
            OPTIONAL { ?area nltl:hullAreaFactor ?areaFactor . }
            ?areaFactor qudt:numericValue ?areaValue .
            ?areaFactor qudt:unit ?unit .
            $this nltl:selectedHullAreaFactor ?selectedFactor .
            ?selectedFactor qudt:numericValue ?selectedValue .
            ?selectedFactor qudt:unit ?selectedUnit .
            FILTER(?unit = ?selectedUnit) .
            # compute max areaValue
            {
                SELECT (MAX(?areaValue) AS ?maxValue) WHERE {
                    $this nltl:hasSpannedHullArea ?a2 .
                    ?a2 nltl:hullAreaFactor ?f2 .
                    ?f2 qudt:numericValue ?areaValue .
                    ?f2 qudt:unit ?unit .
                }
            }
            FILTER(?selectedValue = ?maxValue)
        }""" ;
    ] .

We also need to handle case where no spanned hull area? Possibly no constraint. It says event that structural member spans across boundary, so only apply when there is at least one spanned hull area. So we need to ensure that if hasSpannedHullArea exists, the condition applies. In SPARQL we already require $this nltl:hasSpannedHullArea ?area, so nan.

We also need to ensure that unit matches; maybe unit is unitless UNITLESS anyway.

Add sh:severity sh:Violation.

Also note unresolved property hullAreaBoundary but not needed.

Thus produce SHACL graph in Turtle.

Include prefixes:

@prefix sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix nltl: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#> .
@prefix qudt: <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/> .
@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> . maybe not needed.

Define shape as ex:StructuralMemberLargestHullAreaFactorShape.

Don't invent new IRIs beyond base? It's fine.

We must record ambiguity: unresolved ownership for hullAreaBoundary but not used.

Make sure to use exact IRIs for numeric and unit predicates: from quantityEncoding: numeric_predicate = http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/numericValue; unit_predicate = http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/unit.

Thus using full IRIs.

Now produce final answer with <BEGIN_SHACL> line, then Turtle, then <END_SHACL>.
